The query in `1result.sql` is the most reliable:

• It returns exactly the same set of faculty members as the other two queries (so it satisfies the task).  
• It uses a window function with `RANK()` to select the closest salary per rank, which naturally handles ties without relying on exact floating‑point equality (unlike the other two queries that join on `ABS(..)=min_diff`, which can mis‑match if tiny rounding errors occur).  
• It keeps the output columns in the correct data types (no unnecessary `printf` string formatting).

